# Security, OIDC & sessions

## OIDC issuer

- Mount at issuer root (`:3010`), not under `/api`
- `COOKIE_DOMAIN=localhost` in dev so :3011 login resumes interaction on :3010
- PKCE required; public clients are `trusted_first_party` for auto-consent
- Access token `aud` = `OIDC_DEFAULT_RESOURCE` (resource indicators)
- Token endpoint rate-limited per IP (F35)

## Sessions (hosted login)

| Cookie | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `userAccessToken` / `userRefreshToken` | End-user session (httpOnly) |
| `user-xsrf-token` | CSRF double-submit |
| `adminAccessToken` / `adminRefreshToken` / `xsrf-token` | Operator session |

State-changing browser API calls require matching XSRF header.

## Resource servers (consumers)

- Copy `libs/auth/jwt-resource.guard.ts` — JWKS verify, no introspection
- Map `sub` → local `user_identities` in consumer DB only
- Do not add marketplace authorization here

## CORS

- `CorsOriginsService` merges `CORS_ORIGINS` + active OAuth client origins
- Refresh cache after client URI changes (5 min TTL auto)

## Rate limits

In-memory for dev/single instance. Use Redis before horizontal scale.

## Headers

`applySecurityHeaders` on backend; SolidStart `middleware.ts` on frontends. CSP deferred (Vite HMR).

See [docs/SECURITY.md](../../docs/SECURITY.md).
